# Text formatting: a part of a line in another color or font, written [text]{style} and styled with a For style rule.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Text formatting · Styled parts
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For style: source
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Mono
				Size: 9
				Color: muted
		For style: result
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 14 0
			Typography:
				Size: 13
				Line height: 18
				Markup: markdown
		For style: price
			Typography:
				Color: #B3261E
				Bold: true
		For style: brand
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Serif
				Italic: true
		For style: tag
			Typography:
				Case: uppercase
				Letter spacing: 1
				Weight: 600
				Color: accent
		For style: light
			Typography:
				Weight: 300
	Section:
		Text: Text formatting
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Styled parts
		Paragraph: With `Markup: markdown`, a text in brackets followed by a style name in braces takes the `For style` rule of that name: color, font, weight, italic, case, small caps and letter spacing. The size and the line height stay those of the box.
			Style: intro
		Text: A subscription to [The Gazette]{brand} costs [€12.50]{price} a month.
			Style: source
		Text: A subscription to [The Gazette]{brand} costs [€12.50]{price} a month.
			Style: result
		Text: [New]{tag} Walnut chair with a wool seat.
			Style: source
		Text: [New]{tag} Walnut chair with a wool seat.
			Style: result
		Text: The marks add to the style: [**12.50 EUR**]{light} and **[12.50 EUR]{light}** are bold even with Weight: 300.
			Style: source
		Text: The marks add to the style: [**12.50 EUR**]{light} and **[12.50 EUR]{light}** are bold even with Weight: 300.
			Style: result
		Text: A link with a styled part: [[see the price]{price}](https://stxt.dev).
			Style: source
		Text: A link with a styled part: [[see the price]{price}](https://stxt.dev).
			Style: result
		Text: The same For style rule can style a whole box
			Style: label
		Text: €12.50
			Style: price
